{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>אח</b> — Rabbi Jonah said: its meaning is 'one.' Others said: its meaning is like 'וְאָמַר אָח' (and say, brother). What seems correct to me: <b>אח</b> is a pa'ul form and the man is the one who acts, as if he said: Behold, the rich cannot redeem their brother, nor their own soul from death — and how will this wealth benefit us?! For there is no man who redeems his brother from death, and not only that but even his own soul; therefore 'וְיָקָר פִּדְיוֹן' (and costly is the redemption). The meaning: and let it cease, that this not be forever."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "Resolved הרב / רבי יונה as 'Rabbi Jonah' based on the named commentator; the last clause 'וְחַדֵּל שֶׁלֹּא יִהְיֶה זֶה לְעוֹלָם' is elliptical and translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:17.499570036Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}